# Riff website editing rules

The user-approved Riff redesign supersedes the previous Swiss / Ghost Border design. Read README.md and docs/IA.md before changing the site.

- Active pages use content/site/pages.json through MarketingDocument. Preserve the approved layout and exact style order unless the user requests a design change.
- Headings use the locally hosted FK Screamer font in sentence case. Body copy uses Geist. No full stops at the end of headings. No arrows in CTAs.
- Hero: purple through blue to mint; six cards surrounding Riff. Play its entrance once and keep the cards visible.
- Major colored components and customer quote panels have square corners; inner interface cards may be rounded.
- Feature animations move forward, restart from their initial state after a two-second hold, pause offscreen, and honor reduced-motion settings.
- Navigation: How it works (/#overview), Customers, Pricing, FAQs, Blog. Actions: Sign in, Sign up, Book a demo. Podcast is out of scope.
- Keep legal document wording unchanged without explicit authorization. The approved source matches the previous live legal text, including the October 3, 2026 terms.
- Blog posts remain editable Markdown in content/posts. Never publish a draft through the archive, a direct route, or the sitemap.
- Keep security headers and canonical metadata. Never put credentials or local environment files into source control.
- Do not apply unused legacy Swiss components or Tailwind styles to the active design.
